# What the gates add over a donor-level test: four analyzers on validation v1's cards
# (exploratory; plan committed before the run at d3db111: validation/exploratory/v1_analyzers_plan.md)
# key 7bb8eab615c44438ebbd20582b58d6caeeba2f9ec57f313e40dc8dd846c4286b; pilot.json sha256 485bcf3cdd61394bcec3e58587c73f9e3e6e2afb98d1ab71d635340c49b22a57; per-card results sha256 ceaa8b36fc7708c9baa68717048874f13a7a13ffafb0fc9bcb5ce4934be2aae9
# cards 10540 of 10540; datasets rebuilt 9750, identical to the manifest's 9750

(a) cells
(b) donors, no gates
(c) engine, GATE 0/2/4/5 off
(d) full engine
Changes after the plan (none to the analyzers, the sample or the outcomes; the code was tested on the
first 20 and 60 datasets, and the summary's grouping (section 0) was added after a look at the first
3,200 cards): section 4 leaves out N6a, whose random metric cannot agree by construction, and compares
Monte Carlo p values by their detection only; '-' marks an outcome an analyzer cannot give.

'effect': (a), (b) p < 0.05 in the claimed direction; (c), (d) SUPPORTED. 'against': p < 0.05 the other
way; (c), (d) NOT SUPPORTED, opposite direction. Rates are k/n (95% Clopper-Pearson interval).

